L147: # Assets and characters
L148: 
L149: Reuse library media in chats, organize collections, and reference characters and smart entities.
L150: 
L151: Copy page Copy page
L152: 
L153: fal Agent uses 【54†fal Assets】, your media library on fal. Open the library at 【72†fal.ai/assets】. Assets access follows your account’s enablement and organization policy. This page covers using Assets in a chat. For the full library guide, start with 【54†Introduction to fal Assets】.
L154: ## Automatic registration
L155: 
L156: Supported media attachments are registered as library uploads, and generated media is linked to its chat. The Assets browser displays images, video, audio, and 3D. Agent documents have their own 【73†project workflow】. Open Assets, or use the `@` picker’s Assets tab, to find available media from earlier work. Media remains subject to its retention policy.
L157: ## Reuse in a chat
L158: 
L159:   * Type `@` and open the Assets tab to attach any library item.
L160:   * Open Generations in the palette to refer to an output from this chat.
L161:   * Drag a tile from the media rail into the composer, or use Attach to chat on the tile.
L162: 
L163: ## Search
L164: 
L165: The agent can search your library on your behalf. It searches by text, by image similarity, and by video similarity. Ask for what you remember:
L166: 
L167:     `Find the warehouse shots from last week and use the widest one as the background.
L168:     `
L169: ## Collections
L170: 
L171: A collection is a named group of assets. The agent can create collections, add assets to them, and list what they hold. Add a collection to a project to make its contents part of the project context.
L172: ## Characters and smart entities
L173: Assets supports characters, props, environments, styles, and scenes. Each smart entity has one to twenty reference images and an `@handle`. Characters also require a description. Select an entity from the `@` picker to give the agent reusable visual references for a generation. References help guide the result. Consistency depends on the selected model and its inputs. See 【74†Characters and smart entities】 for the entity types and 【75†Using entities in generations】 for model-specific behavior.
L174:     `Put @mara in a rain-soaked alley at night, then animate a slow dolly-in.
L175:     `
L176: The agent can create a character for you from images in the chat, or you can create one in Assets. Character cards in the chat show the portrait, the handle, the bio, and the collections the character appears in. The character-design 【76†skill】 adds reference sheets, expression sheets, and outfit variations.
L177: ## Media lifetime
L178: 
L179: Files follow the lifetime applied to them. See 【51†Agent retention】 for chat policies and 【60†Assets retention and deletion】 for the difference between removing library items and deleting media files.
